From: EglantinePS5
Subject: [PATCH] up: EDEN_UP_WAIT_RECLAIM's emergency pass (the front's switch, off unless set): a thread that waits for memory while no frame is drawn gets graphics memory freed on the GPU thread, between two entries

Why: run1441/run1442 (T179, 13 Nov) died at the load past the field with a thread waiting 10 s for one
2 MiB block. No frame was drawn during the wait (the driver's memory lines stop at t=212 s, the texture
cache's last TickFrame at 217.5 s, the wait ran 216.4-226.5 s), and the collector, the pressure drain and
the area evictor run only at frame ends; the collector ages images by frames. The driver held about
4 GiB (images 2.3 GiB) the whole time.

What: the front (src/guest_memory_service.inc, T181a) calls eden_wait_reclaim_request(seq, target, age,
gpu_ms) from a helper thread of its own (never from the fault handler) while a thread other than
GPUBack and GPU has waited 50 ms or more. The request queues RasterizerVulkan::WaitReclaimPass with
GPU::RunInOrder: with the split it is a deferred function the back runs between two entries (the back
owns the scheduler there, holds no cache lock, and back_quiet is false while it runs, so the front
cannot use the scheduler at the same time); without the split the GPU thread runs it between
commands. The GPU thread's queue wakes the GPU thread and Publish wakes the back, as for any other
RunInOrder (nx2_gsv uses it from service threads).

The pass (renderer_vulkan/wait_reclaim.h), both cache locks by try_lock only (10 tries 2 ms apart; a
waiting CPU thread may hold one, a download under the texture cache's lock): (a) the pressure drain's
releases (submit, wait for the GPU at most gpu_ms, deleted images it is past, deleted buffers when it
got there, RetryRefusedNow, the staging pool's ReleaseCompleted); (b) TextureCache::WaitReclaimEvict:
images by least-recent use, 1 MiB and larger first, then the rest, until `target` bytes, at most 512,
only images unused for `age` frames (front default 2: not in this frame or the last), not a bound
render target, and with nothing to copy back (LoadHoldEvict's test: decoding, kept async, kept remade
and downloadable GPU-written images stay); then submit and wait again and destroy them; (c) VMA's
device memory before and after (the console's RADV releases memory the GPU is done with at once,
radv_ps5_bo.c radv_ps5_memory_retire; VMA frees empty blocks while the budget reads exceeded), and
with EDEN_UP_DRAIN_TO_POOL=1 own memory for new buffers for 3 s. Nothing while the guest's conditional
rendering is on (as the drain). A GPU wait that ran out: no wait again until the GPU passed that tick
(the drain's behind rule), and no images deleted in that pass.

The front reads the result with eden_wait_reclaim_stats and writes the lines. The rasterizer registers
itself for requests in its constructor and leaves in its destructor (one pointer under a mutex). No
request (the default): nothing here runs. No file here is a translation id input and no name is added
to TranslationSwitches: KEEPS THE STORE.

